WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:10.840
Request from Ichigo... when watching the television, sit a safe distance from the television in a well-lit room.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.230
Ever since I've returned to Paris, I've been doing my best as part of this team.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.840
I'm surprised that we're to battle right off the bat,

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:15.410
but this time, I'm going to fight against you fair and square, and win!

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.810
Lemon-chan...

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.990
Yeah! Let's both do our best!

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.910
Though, I'm impressed, Rick.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.090
You were quick to make friends with Ichigo-senpai just as she arrived here!

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.000
I can't leave cute girls alone, you see.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.090
Ichigo-senpai, Rick is an amazing genius.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:41.310
There's probably no one better than him in the Paris campus at making sweets suited to women.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:45.850
Perhaps I should whip up some wonderful sweets in your image, Ichigo?

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.280
Clara, who came from Germany, has the best grades in school, and specializes in statistics.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.720
She's the "brain" of our team.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:57.320
Greetings.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.780
OP sequence

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.940
And Eli here hails from Great Britain.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.310
Being in a family that runs a perfume company, she has a wonderful nose!

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.120
You could call her a scent sommelier!

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.130
It seems like you have quite the international team there.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:14.840
Thanks to them, the variations of sweets we can make have increased a lot!

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.340
How nice...

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:21.010
As expected from the main Paris campus... It's on a different scale from its Japanese counterpart!

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.990
Oh yes, we haven't introduced ourselves yet.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:25.520
I'm...

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.520
We know you already.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.250
Hanabusa Satsuki, specializing in detailed Sweets Crafts.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.130
The chocolate master, Kashino Makoto.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.950
Andou Sennosuke, who wants to combine traditional Japanese and Western confectioneries.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:43.270
Collectively known as the "Sweets Princes" on the Japanese campus, the talents of whom even the teachers have taken notice of.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.580
You're quite informed...

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:50.030
Not only you. I have gathered information on all the participants here.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.300
Except for you, Amano Ichigo.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.220
Me?

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:57.800
It seems you got transferred into the academy from Henri-sensei's personal recommendation,

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.920
despite not having any particular talents in making sweets.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.020
And yet, you gathered powerful members and became their leader.

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:08.550
You are truly beyond expectations, in many senses of the word.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.520
I've nothing to say for myself...

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.930
Well...

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:19.140
I think that mysterious girls are more attractive.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.530
I garner more interest in you by the second, Ichigo.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.740
What a pompous bastard. I can't stand his type.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.740
Pretty sure he's insecure deep inside, though.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.820
You must be the Spirits for the opposing team, yes?

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.160
Nice to meet you. I am Rick's Spirit, Basil.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.170
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.930
This is Clara's Spirit.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.950
I am Estragon.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.130
Too bad you won't make it past the first round.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.310
We won't know that until we try!

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.980
And this is Elizabeth's Spirit, Laurier.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.670
This is Lemon's Spirit.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.940
I'm Mint! Nice to meet you!

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.940
I am Satsuki's Spirit, Cafe.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.850
I'm Andou's Spirit, Caramel!

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.710
I am Kashino's Spirit, Chocolat!

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.040
And I'm Ichigo's Spirit, Vanilla!

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.960
You're Ichigo-senpai's Spirit?

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.000
Yes, that's me...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.360
I've heard about you from Lemon!

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.240
She said that she was sure Ichigo-senpai would have a splendid Spirit partner!

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:24.470
I'm so glad I could meet you, Vanilla-senpai!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.050
V-Vanilla-senpai?

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.440
The theme for the first round is a "Food Wagon".

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.690
After we decide on the menu, we need to go get ingredients and equipment.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.400
We'll also be doing all the serving.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.550
Furthermore, we have to make a profit.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:50.510
The team who sells the most over the competition will be declared the winner.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:01.130
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:01.130
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:06.500
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:06.500
I'll give you happiness, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:12.040
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, hapinesu made go!

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:12.040
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, Happiness made go!

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:17.210
chansu no tobira aketa toki kara kibun joujou ↑ ↑

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:17.210
Since I opened the door of chance, my mood lifted.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:21.170
youkoso suiitsu no oukoku he

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:21.170
Welcome to the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.050
Bon appétit!

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:29.420
hajimehane, hetappi demo megezu ni hibishoujin<i>!</i>

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:29.420
Though I was terrible at the beginning, I was diligent everyday<i>!</i>

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.100
「makeruna<i>! atashi」</i>

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.100
「I won't lose<i>!</i> I said to myself」

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.070
Courage!

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:39.850
My dream migakeba hikaru takaramono

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:39.850
My dream when polished is a shining treasure.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.610
fairy chikara kashite<i>!</i>

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.610
Fairy, lend me your strength<i>!</i>

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:47.980
shifon, se shibon, juré, bonjuuru, hatsuratsu furuutsu, raburii made go!

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:47.980
Chiffon, C'est si bon, Gelée, Bonjour, Lively fruits, Lovely made go!

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:54.120
nakitaku natte mo egao ni nareru mahou

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:54.120
Even if you cry, there is magic that can make you smile.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:59.300
「oishii<i>!」 wo tsukurutte omoikkiri tanoshii ne</i>

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:59.300
「Delicious<i>!</i>」 and making it wholeheartedly is fun.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:05.340
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:05.340
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.680
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.680
I'll give happiness to you, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:15.230
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, fun fun

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:15.230
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, fun, fun

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.440
yume ni eeru<i>!</i>

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.440
Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.870
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:30.280
It's a lovely morning. Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:37.920
recipe 41

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:37.920
The Fourth Sweets Prince?

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.020
Morning...

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.200
Good morning, Ichigo-chan.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.240
Morning. Looks like you slept well.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.200
You're late! Here!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.500
What's this?

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.850
You're in charge of breakfast.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.730
I was!?

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:54.750
Breakfast Duty
Monday  Ichigo
Tuesday  Kashino
Wednesday  Andou
Thursday  Hanabusa
Friday  Ichigo
Saturday  Kashino
Sunday  Andou

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.910
You're right! I totally forgot!

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:00.930
Sheesh! You're making everyone hungry!

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.460
Hurry up and do it!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.350
Ichigo, I'll help too!

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:06.970
I'll make some café au lait.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.820
What should I make?

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:14.830
Actually, I don't really have that much experience making breakfast.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:15.980
That's it!

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.480
Take some eggs...

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.730
Mix with milk and fresh cream...

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.190
A bit of sugar, and...

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.330
Mix it up nice and good.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.930
I know! You're making French toast!

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:27.900
Correct!

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.680
Kaorina Magical Macaroni!

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.620
Potopoto Potorino!

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:43.340
Put the mixture in a large pan, soak the bread slices thoroughly, and then stick them in a preheated oven!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.050
Huh? That's strange...

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.170
What's the matter, Ichigo-chan?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.150
This oven isn't hot at all.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.930
That oven uses Fahrenheit.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.970
We use Celsius in Japan.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.720
You see ovens like this overseas sometimes.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:05.230
Hmm, 180 degrees Celsius should be about 360 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.150
If we wait for a bit, the oven should warm up.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.220
It's not heating up?

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.450
This thing is broken.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.850
But I prepared all that French toast!

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:23.100
It'll be a pain, but let's cook them on the hot plate.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.460
Okay...

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.400
Does anyone have a pocket flashlight?

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.470
We don't have professional tools here... You won't be able to fix it.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.650
We've got to!

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:37.840
The Grand Prix match is in three days!

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.180
We're screwed if the oven is broken!

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.560
Hey, let me try!

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.550
It turned on!

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.360
Amano, great job!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.700
I fix the TV screen whenever it goes funny at home, just like this.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.580
Isn't it getting a little <i>too</i> hot?

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.380
A-Amano, get away from the oven!

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.760
I managed to save the French toast, at least.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.220
Cafe-kun, a mirror, a mirror!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.360
Here, Satsuki.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.970
I've got a soot beard like some criminal!!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.140
This can't be me!!

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.300
That was scary...

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.150
Y-You're heavy...

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.170
I-I'm not that heavy!

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:39.840
Idiot... Take a look.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.660
Shards of glass?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:46.650
Man, you're so careless, Amano.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.290
T-Thank you...

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.700
Someone's coming!

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:56.890
It's the landlady!

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.470
This is bad!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.750
She must've heard that huge explosion and came running!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.100
What'll we do?

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.090
If she sees that, she'll kick us out of this apartment!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.050
Y-Yes, I'm coming!

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.200
What the heck was that explosion!?

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:22.040
We're sorry! We tried to use the oven, and...

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.540
W-We'll pay for the oven, we promise!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.150
We'll also make this kitchen as good as new!

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.540
So...

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.550
Please don't kick us out of the apartment!

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:39.220
After you've finished breakfast, come and see me.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:45.480
What are we going to do? She's gonna kick us out!

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.240
Welcome!

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.460
Please go ahead and sample anything that you'd like!

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:11.380
So, what do you think of my French toast?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.460
It's too sweet.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.050
You should've predicted that we'd put syrup and stuff on afterwards,

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.470
and so held off on the sweetening in the first place.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:22.650
The eggs are cooked unevenly.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.970
I'd give it a 62% overall.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.980
It's like I have three mother-in-laws...

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.940
Now then, we're having a food wagon competition,

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.980
so I was thinking of something like this.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.360
Salade de Fruits, is it?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.690
In this country, people drink wine instead of water,

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:42.070
so there should be quite a few people that like fruit, right?

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.950
This would be better than some frozen sweets!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:49.620
Delicious, aren't they? I was thinking of selling them one euro a cup.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.900
One euro?

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.290
That's too cheap!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.550
We'd need to charge four euro for these ingredients...

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.860
Exactly! We'll sell top-quality fruit at outrageous prices!

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.930
We're sure to sell a ton that way!

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.120
I don't think it'll be that easy.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:06.080
This battle will require a careful cost analysis.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:09.350
Oh? Did you forget who you're talking to?

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:13.150
If need be, I can manipulate the market prices just like <i>that!</i>

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.460
Oh, yeah. You could.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:23.340
You did go so far as to buy up our St. Marie Academy's Principality of Andorra campus in order to participate in this Grand Prix, after all.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.370
Château confectionery is a worldwide business, after all!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:36.670
If I win this competition, even Makoto-kun will be forced to recognise me!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.460
Watch me, Makoto-kun!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:04.140
Henri-sensei did tell me to call him if I ever got in trouble, right?

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.620
Let me consult him...

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:09.620
Yes?

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:12.860
I'm sorry! I must have the wrong number.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.570
This is Henri Lucas's cellphone.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:17.290
Who am I speaking to?

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.960
Umm, my name is Amano Ichigo.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:22.560
I am his secretary, Sully.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.870
Henri is currently in a meeting.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.300
I can leave him a message if you'd like.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.720
I don't really have a message, but...

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.630
Umm...

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:31.230
Yes?

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:34.520
Is Henri-sensei busy every day?

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:36.360
Let's see...

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:42.150
He's involved in a large project right now, so his schedule is fully packed.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.370
It sure is dusty...

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:53.980
So this place used to be a shop?

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.170
The shutter was always closed, so I didn't notice.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:01.650
This was called Glaces. In other words, a shop that sold gelato.

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:06.560
My husband and I started it up twenty years ago.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:13.820
It was very busy with all the preparation and reception, but every day was so fulfilling.

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:15.980
However...

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:22.860
Three years ago, my husband passed away, which immediately led to my decision of the shop's closure.

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:29.100
I never really had the skills for making gelato myself, you see.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:34.870
At the very least, my daughter Emma did manage to make it in St. Marie Academy.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.900
St. Marie Academy?

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:43.970
However, after she graduated, she said she didn't want to take over the shop, and got a normal job instead.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.300
I see.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:54.120
From my daughter's perspective, living her whole life cooped up in this tiny gelato shop must have seemed really boring.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:55.560
Ah, here we go.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.960
I'll let you borrow this.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.990
It's a business use vacuum cleaner.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.730
With this, you can clean up that soot in a second.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.490
Thank you very much!

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.940
We'll borrow it, then!

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.450
And, I'm sorry...

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.810
About the oven.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:15.040
If I had maintained it properly, this wouldn't have happened.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.050
No, she's the one who killed it off...

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.040
Do you <i>have</i> to look at me like that?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:24.050
You will all become great pâtissiers when you graduate, right?

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.270
Yes!

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.940
That's the spirit.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:31.870
A life lived making delicious sweets for everyone can't be beat.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.460
I'm jealous...

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:35.200
I'm off.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.770
Thank you very much!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:41.100
So she just wanted to lend us her vacuum, eh?

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:44.860
We were panicking over whether we were getting kicked out or not.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.480
Ichigo, is something wrong?

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:48.240
No.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:53.360
Okay, we've borrowed the vacuum, so let's clean up that kitchen!

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:56.160
Yup! <i>Clean cuisine</i>, as they say!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.500
Punilla is here!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.870
Don't call me Punilla!

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.250
Très bien!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:09.050
Just looking at delicious sweets and cute girls is enough to make me happy.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:12.800
Rick, do you have an idea for the food wagon?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:16.180
Let's see... If you go with my tastes...

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:20.850
I don't want to do a crêpe filled with so much cream that it squirts out around a cute girl's mouth...

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.460
Or some pie where the filling flows out...

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:27.190
We need something that can be eaten neatly.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:31.950
And it also has to be something that a girl can hold while looking cute!

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.720
If we take your opinion and add a little something to it,

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:38.010
plus accounting for the weather and temperature forecast that day,

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:40.660
plus recent trends in what is selling...

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.170
Ring donuts seem to be our best bet.

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:45.510
Ring donuts?

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:47.150
Yes, sounds good!

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:52.250
Fluffy ring donuts with a pink strawberry-chocolate coating.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:56.180
Sprinkle on some sugar and wrap it nice and cute...

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:03.380
I think that such cute donuts will attract the Parisien's taste for new fads.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:03.380
TL Note: Le Parisien is a French daily newspaper.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:05.400
Eli, do you agree? How about you, Clara?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:10.560
Yes. I have confidence in the answer that my computer gave me.

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:14.410
Then it's decided. Let's hurry and get the ingredients.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.340
Whoa there. I'll handle that.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:22.760
As a man, I can't make you girls carry heavy things.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:28.500
Wake up!

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.510
What!?

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.760
I'm still sleepy...

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:36.980
Me too...

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.120
Wait, did we leave Chocolat behind?

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.020
She's in here.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.520
Another fifteen minutes...

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:49.180
Wow, she can actually sleep in there?

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.840
That's Chocolat for you.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.340
A morning market, huh? Sounds interesting.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:56.810
Yeah. The landlady gave me this tip.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:58.750
She told me to check it out.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.490
We take a right over there.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:05.790
This is the market, right?

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:09.650
Look at all the roses!

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:13.000
France grows many rare varieties of roses.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.890
I found a yummy-looking watermelon!

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:19.180
And they're selling bread over there!

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:22.640
It seems Amano-san prefers food over flowers.

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:27.350
Okay everyone, try and find me!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.950
Umm...

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:31.750
Found you!

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.360
You found me...

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.560
You were trying to hide there?

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:36.950
You couldn't stand out more!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.070
Fine, then it's your turn to hide next, Chocolat!

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:41.710
Fine by me!

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:44.750
Try and find me if you can!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.930
They'll never find me in here...

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.980
It's escargot!!

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.260
Found you, Chocolat!

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.310
Delicious!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:08.170
Right, I haven't had anything since this morning...

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.220
Yeah, if you don't count that you sampled everything here already...

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:12.410
Have you no shame?

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:15.260
Those nibbles alone won't satisfy me!

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:20.120
So then, has anyone thought of an idea for our food wagon?

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:24.810
Well, I do have something in mind that I'd like to try...

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:30.330
But it's not something I've made before, so I don't know if I can make it right...

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.540
Wait, could that be...

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.960
Gelato?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.030
Exactly!

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:36.320
How did you know?

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.510
Looks like we were all thinking the same thing.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:45.060
The landlady told us yesterday that she'd love to make delicious gelato for everyone,

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.020
so I've been thinking about it ever since.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:49.960
Us too!

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:50.610
Me too!

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:53.900
Then it's decided... We'll make gelato for the food wagon match!

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.260
If it's decided, then...

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.390
Ichigo!

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:58.650
Hey!

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.350
Rick!

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:03.660
It must be fate that brought us together again at a place like this!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:05.660
It's the lady-killer...

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.560
Did you come here for shopping as well, Ichigo?

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:09.310
Yeah...

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:12.970
As did I! I just finished up, actually.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:17.300
I know! The weather is lovely out, so let's go on a date now!

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.270
Come, sit behind me.

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:22.580
Uh... Well...

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:25.060
What's with you?

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:30.510
Sorry, but Ichigo-chan is going shopping with us.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:32.550
So she hasn't the time to date you.

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:34.890
Well, this just doesn't sit right.

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:41.730
She has three knights, so it's not necessary to make a lady go out shopping as well, is it?

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:45.740
Or are Japanese men really that weak?

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.520
Try me!

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:51.910
Amano-san came to Paris to participate in the World Cake Grand Prix!

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:54.610
She doesn't have time for a fling with someone like you.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:58.800
I don't like you saying things like "fling."

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:04.160
The way I look at it, both love and desserts should be sweet.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:10.510
And besides, I invited <i>Ichigo</i>, so your opinions on the matter are irrelevant.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:15.470
Unless, that is, one of you is her boyfriend.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:17.730
In that case I'll politely back off.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.260
Ichigo?

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.770
Are you currently dating someone?

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:25.060
No! Not at all!

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:25.950
Thank goodness!

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:29.920
Well then, if my team wins this match...

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:32.290
Ichigo, be my girlfriend.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.560
Hey, wait!

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.400
Amano-san isn't a trophy!

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:39.340
Treating her like some object is rude!

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:42.960
What's rude is you thinking that's what I meant!

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:51.600
It so happens that we Italians are people that love to wager, like on the gladiators in the Colosseum during the reign of the Roman Empire!

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:58.310
If you really are knights that wish to protect Ichigo, then all you have to do is win this competition.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:04.990
I suppose I'll back off from these big scary knights and go back peacefully for today.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:11.290
I'll be sure to win this match and make Ichigo my girlfriend.

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.440
Ciao!

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.840
You've gotta be kidding me!

